 "label": "Washing and grooming",
 "topic": "Body & health",
 "rationale": "Looking after your body day to day: washing your hands, face and hair, and cutting your hair and nails.",
 "mixUps": "arau covers every kind of washing, from hands to hair, so there's no separate shampoo verb. The kiru in kami o kiru and tsume o kiru means cut (kitta), not wear (fuku o kiru, kita), and kami kitta is said even when a stylist cut it.",
